{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.KZ.KZHalfMonodromy","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.KZ.KZHalfMonodromy","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.KZ.KZComplex","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.Analytic.IsolatedZeros","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.Complex.CauchyIntegral"],"declarations":20,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.KZ.KZHalfMonodromy.half_monodromy","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.KZ.KZHalfMonodromy.half_monodromy","kind":"theorem","line":234,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/KZ/KZHalfMonodromy.lean#L234-L384","doc":"**Half-monodromy.** Pulling the solution of `KZ(C, A)` normalised at `1` (with\n`C = −A − B`) back along `z ↦ 1/(1 − z)` gives the solution of `KZ(A, B)` normalised at `0`,\ntimes `e^{−iπA}`, throughout the region `T`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.KZ.KZHalfMonodromy.isKZSolOn_pullback","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.KZ.KZHalfMonodromy.isKZSolOn_pullback","kind":"theorem","line":218,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/KZ/KZHalfMonodromy.lean#L218-L232","doc":"`G₁^{CA}(1/(1−z))`, pulled back twice along `ρ`, solves `KZ(A, B)` on `T`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.KZ.KZHalfMonodromy.rho_rho_mem_D₁","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.KZ.KZHalfMonodromy.rho_rho_mem_D₁","kind":"theorem","line":204,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/KZ/KZHalfMonodromy.lean#L204-L216","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.KZ.KZHalfMonodromy.norm_neg_div_lt_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.KZ.KZHalfMonodromy.norm_neg_div_lt_one","kind":"theorem","line":196,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-obs